      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityneighborhoods.nyc/westerleigh"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1923 the Staten Island Parks Department built a large octagonal bandstand in Westerleigh Park, where summer concerts still echo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westerleighparkscoalition.com/history-of-westerleigh"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Westerleigh Collegiate Institute opened its doors in 1895, becoming the neighborhood’s first public high school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westerleighparkscoalition.com/history-of-westerleigh"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Perched on high ground, Westerleigh offers clear views of Newark and even farther on sunny days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westerleigh%2C_Staten_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "South of the expressway, Ingram Woods preserves a slice of Staten Island’s original forest as an undeveloped park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
